            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did pai mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: வண்டி",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வண்டி (vaṇḍi) — \"a vehicle, a cart\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The general word for a thing with wheels. A bullock cart is a வண்டி (vaṇḍi); so is a bicycle, and so is a car. Tamil starts here and adds a word in front when it needs to be exact."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In the middle sits ண்ட — the curled-back ண closed by a புள்ளி and leaning on ட. That pair is one of the most common shapes in the language, and you will now start seeing it everywhere."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word the rest of this chapter is built on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "vaṇḍi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *vaṇḍi*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, curling the tongue back for the ண",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, curling the tongue back for the ண]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say vāṅgu, then say pai, then say vaṇḍi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *vāṅgu*, then say *pai*, then say *vaṇḍi*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does வண்டி (vaṇḍi) mean? (\"A vehicle, a cart\".)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
