            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: read வண்டி (vaṇḍi), and say what it means."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ரயில்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ரயில் (rayil) — \"a train\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A borrowed word, and it wears the borrowing openly: English \"rail\", written straight out in Tamil letters."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "There is a clue in the very first letter. Tamil words do not normally begin with ர, so a word that starts that way has almost always come in from somewhere else. You now have a small test you can run on a word before anyone tells you where it is from."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three, and one of them is a visitor."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "rayil",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *rayil*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "vaṇḍi, then rayil — and say which one is Tamil's own",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *vaṇḍi*, then *rayil* — and say which one is Tamil's own]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say pērundu, then read வண்டி (vaṇḍi), then say rayil",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *pērundu*, then read **வண்டி**, then say *rayil*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does the ர at the front tell you about ரயில் (rayil)? (That it is a borrowed word.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
