            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did sālai mean, and what did rayil mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: நிலையம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "நிலையம் (nilaiyam) — \"a station\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The place where the vehicle stands still."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Inside it is நிலை (nilai) — \"standing, state\" — and you have met that piece before without being told. It is sitting inside வானிலை (vāṉilai), the weather, which is literally the sky's state. One small piece, two words that could hardly be further apart."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is worth more than the word itself: Tamil builds long words out of short ones you already own, and from here on you can start looking for the pieces."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the chapter runs end to end."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
